#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/01-iot_esp8266_config.rst:18
msgid "1.0 Configuring the ESP8266"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/01-iot_esp8266_config.rst:20
msgid "The ESP8266 module that comes with the kit is already pre-burned with AT firmware, but you still need to modify its configuration by following the steps below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/01-iot_esp8266_config.rst:23
msgid "Build the circuit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/01-iot_esp8266_config.rst:28
msgid "Open the ``00-Set_software_serial.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_esp01\\wifi\\00-Set_software_serial``. Or copy this code into Arduino IDE. And upload the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/01-iot_esp8266_config.rst:30
msgid "The code establishes a software serial communication using Arduino's SoftwareSerial library, allowing the Arduino to communicate with the ESP8266 module through its digital pins 2 and 3 (as Rx and Tx). It checks for data transfer between them, forwarding received messages from one to the other at a baud rate of 115200. **With this code, you can use the Arduino's serial monitor to send AT firmware commands to the ESP8266 module and receive its responses.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/01-iot_esp8266_config.rst:53
msgid "Click the magnifying glass icon (Serial Monitor) in the upper right corner and set the baud rate to **115200**. (You may have some printed information like me, or you may not, it doesn’t matter, just go to the next step.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/01-iot_esp8266_config.rst:59
msgid "If ``ready`` doesn't appear, you can try to reset the ESP8266 module(connect RST to GND) and re-open the Serial Monitor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/01-iot_esp8266_config.rst:61
msgid "In addition, if the result is ``OK``, you may need to re-burn the firmware, please refer to :ref:`burn_firmware` for details. If you still can't solve it, please take a screenshot of the serial monitor and send it to service@sunfounder.com, we will help you solve the problem as soon as possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/01-iot_esp8266_config.rst:63
msgid "Click on **NEWLINE DROPDOWN BOX**, select ``both NL & CR`` in the drop down option, enter ``AT``, if it returns OK, it means ESP8266 has successfully established connection with R4 board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/01-iot_esp8266_config.rst:69
msgid "Enter ``AT+CWMODE=3`` and the managed mode will be changed to **Station and AP** coexistence."
msgstr ""

